        "original_id": "19c2f5c8-ea4b-5a02-8725-ccd51fe13e3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Schlegel, Frank De Winne, Dirk Frimout, Pål Brekke\n- Organizations: ESA, NASA, Belgian Air Component, Roscosmos\n- Missions and Projects: Space Shuttle missions, ISS Expedition 21, Expedition 35, SOHO\n- Places: Überlingen, Ledeberg, Belgium, NASA Goddard Space Flight Center\n- Roles: astronaut, physicist, officer, commander, Deputy Project Scientist\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Schlegel was born in Überlingen on 3 August 1951.\n- Hans Schlegel is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Frank De Winne was born on 25 April 1961 in Ledeberg, Belgium.\n- Frank De Winne is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\n- In 1999, Pål Brekke joined ESA as the SOHO Deputy Project Scientist stationed at NASA Goddard Space Flight Center.\n- In 2009, Frank De Winne commanded ISS Expedition 21 and became the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission.\n- Frank De Winne was Belgium's second person in space after Dirk Frimout.\n- Expedition 35 was only the second ISS crew led by neither a NASA astronaut nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 under Frank De Winne's command in 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9dd8f235-48c3-531c-8f78-75adc36994c1",
        "text": "Page: Hans Schlegel. Sentence: Hans Wilhelm Schlegel (Überlingen, 3 August 1951) is a German physicist, an ESA astronaut, and a veteran of two NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: Frank, Viscount De Winne (born 25 April 1961, in Ledeberg, Belgium) is a Belgian Air Component officer and an ESA astronaut.\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He is Belgium's second person in space (after Dirk Frimout).\nPage: Frank De Winne. Sentence: He was the first ESA astronaut to command a space mission when he served as commander of ISS Expedition 21.\nPage: Expedition 35. Sentence: Expedition 35 was also only the second time an ISS crew is led by neither a NASA astronaut, nor a Roscosmos cosmonaut, after Expedition 21 in 2009, when ESA astronaut Frank De Winne was in command.\nPage: Pål Brekke. Sentence: In 1999 he joined the European Space Agency (ESA) as the SOHO Deputy Project Scientist stationed at NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center.",
